{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I’ll be helping take care of you tonight. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve had green stuff coming out of my trach for three days, and I’m coughing a lot. I feel chills, and my chest hurts when I breathe. My throat’s sore too, and it’s hard to swallow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. No fever at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not that I checked, but I didn’t feel hot. Just the chills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. You’ve been through this before, right? Similar symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, just like last time. I thought it might be infection again, so I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray and some blood work. The X-ray looks clear—no pneumonia. Your white blood cell count is normal, and you’re not running a fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It doesn’t look like it. Your symptoms are very similar to your last admission, when we found no infection. We think this might be from dryness in your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the green mucus? That always worries me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Green mucus can happen even without infection, especially with chronic tracheostomy. It’s often from irritation or dryness. We’re not seeing signs of active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… but I’m in pain. My throat and chest hurt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. We gave you some oxycodone earlier. Is it helping at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little, but I think morphine works better for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can switch to morphine if that’s what helps. I’ll order it now for your comfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. Also, I know I’m supposed to use the humidifier more, but sometimes I forget or it’s just hard to keep up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay to admit. The interventional pulmonology team will come by tomorrow to go over your trach care again. Using the HME—like the Thermovent—during the day really helps keep your airway moist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel better when I use it. I just need to remember."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2167-05-28 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you have plenty of supplies when you go home. Apria is already set up to send them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures came back—no growth. That’s another sign there’s no active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So we’re sure it’s not bacteria again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Pretty sure. No fever, normal labs, clear chest X-ray. We’re not continuing antibiotics. Your symptoms seem tied to airway dryness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the sputum test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The sputum was contaminated with mouth secretions, so we can’t trust the results. But given everything else, we don’t think it changes the picture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My pain’s better with the morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2167-05-29 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep managing your pain. The pulmonologist will stop by later to reinforce trach care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2167-05-29 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The IP team visited. They reminded you about using the HME daily and changing it every 24 hours, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2167-05-29 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they showed me again. I’ll try to be more consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2167-05-29 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask. Your breathing is stable, and you’re not getting worse—actually, you seem a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2167-05-29 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel less tight in my chest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2167-05-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your repeat labs are stable. Hemoglobin’s a bit low but not new. We’re still calling it a hemoglobinopathy—likely thalassemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2167-05-30 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I’m always a little anemic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2167-05-30 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It’s not iron deficiency. Your iron studies are fine. This is genetic. We’ll suggest genetic testing to confirm the type."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2167-05-30 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should my family know?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2167-05-30 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially siblings. We’ll include that in your follow-up plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2167-05-30 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if everything stays the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2167-05-30 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will I keep using the same meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2167-05-30 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—same pain meds, same trach care, same reflux and breathing treatments. No antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2167-05-31 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Keep using the HME daily, stay on your regular meds, and call Apria if supplies don’t arrive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2167-05-31 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2167-05-31 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Pulmonology, ENT, and your primary team. We’ll also refer you to pain clinic for long-term management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2167-05-31 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll try to stick with the humidifier this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2167-05-31 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to support you. Take care, and call if symptoms change."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2167-05-28 19:50:00",
    "admission_end": "2167-05-31 12:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A young woman with congenital tracheobronchomalacia and tracheostomy status was admitted for increased green sputum, cough, pleuritic chest pain, and throat pain. She had recent hospitalizations for Staph lugdunensis bacteremia and MRSA tracheitis. Evaluation revealed no fever, normal white blood cell count, clear chest X-ray, and negative blood cultures. Sputum was contaminated and uninterpretable. Given the lack of infection markers and similarity to prior non-infectious episodes, symptoms were attributed to airway irritation from inadequate humidification. Antibiotics were withheld, pain was managed with opioids, and interventional pulmonology reinforced tracheostomy care with daily use of a Portex Thermovent® HME. She remained stable, symptoms improved, and she was discharged home with continued trach care, pain management, and follow-up plans. A hemoglobinopathy (likely beta thalassemia) was noted, with genetic testing recommended.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute tracheitis without obstruction",
      "Cough",
      "Congenital bronchomalacia",
      "Congenital tracheomalacia",
      "Other hemoglobinopathies",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Bronchopulmonary dysplasia originating in the perinatal period",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Pleurodynia",
      "Patient's noncompliance with other medical treatment and regimen"
    ]
  }
}
